Z||000001||AusFiero||05-12-2001||11:30 AM||||Well that is  certainly different Loki. Reminds me of a interior I seen online available in Europe somewhere. Is certainly doable (is doable a word). Console and door trims are not too hard to do but dashes can be a nightmare if you dont put some thought into them. I like the look of that style. Unsure on the colour scheme but the shape is definately hot.<P>I have plans to make my next Fiero (always want a better one don't we  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) extremely space age inside. Want to include Sat Navigation with touch screen control, tv, digital displays where needed and hopefully if they get cheap enough touch controls rather than switches on all accessories. Throw in a heads up display (a proper one with no dash gauges at all) and seats/interior shape more suited to a space ship. Kick ass stereo (well not too over the top price wise) and hide all the speakers this time around. <P>Now how to convince the wife I really will need a $12,000 interior in my next Fiero (whats up with this she asks often when I say I wanna build another one. She just doesn't understand these things). Maybe I could sell her car to fund the project. She bitches about me spending money on the Fiero but the lady gets around in a 1999 model Holden Commodore R91 Police Pack. An ex cop car so she can chase me, pull me over and put me in handcuffs and ooops wrong forum...lol  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero.gif"> <BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||1
